      "devdoc": {
        "details": "Last contract of the launch. Its constructor (inside the launch transaction) registers the system's contracts with PLEA and commits to the hook's, the Letterbox's and the Tribunal's exact init code, so the launch transaction stays under Ethereum's 16,777,216-gas cap. After launch, anyone calls `deployHook` with a salt mined off chain (script/MineSalt.s.sol): the hook lands on an address carrying its flag bits, and PLEA mints 82% to it, 6% to Seasons and 12% to the distributor. Anyone calls `deployLetterbox` and `deployTribunal` once each with the committed creation code: both read their settings from this contract. Every result's code and settings are fully determined by the committed code, so front-running any of these calls changes nothing but, for the hook, the address: the salt is the caller's, so a front-runner may land the same hook at another flag-valid address (the Letterbox and the Tribunal use salt 0 and have fixed addresses). A zero Tribunal hash launches with objections off for good. `seed` opens trading once the hook, the Letterbox and a committed Tribunal exist: the owner may call it any time, anyone once `START` has passed.Round 5, R5-A2-1: the Letterbox's (and the Tribunal's) oracle-fee settings are checked here, in the launch transaction, wherever they do not depend on the chain; the one that does (no minted fee on chain id 1) stops `deployLetterbox`, and `seed` waits for the Letterbox, so trading never opens on a launch whose letters could never work.",
        "kind": "dev",
        "methods": {},
        "title": "PleaLaunch \u2014 wires PLEA at launch and deploys the hook, the Letterbox and the Tribunal afterwards",
        "version": 1
      },
      "userdoc": {
        "kind": "user",
        "methods": {
          "FLAGS()": {
            "notice": "beforeInitialize | beforeAddLiquidity | beforeSwap | afterSwap | beforeSwapReturnDelta | afterSwapReturnDelta"
          },
          "START()": {
            "notice": "Latest time trading opens: from then on anyone may call `seed`."
          },
          "deployHook(bytes32,bytes)": {
            "notice": "Deploys PleaHook with CREATE2 at a flagged address and lets PLEA mint the supply. `initCode` must be the committed one (PleaHook creation code + its constructor arguments)."
          },
          "deployLetterbox(bytes)": {
            "notice": "Deploys the Letterbox with CREATE2 (salt 0) and registers it with PLEA, once. `creationCode` must be the committed one; the Letterbox reads its settings from this contract."
          },
          "deployTribunal(bytes)": {
            "notice": "Deploys the Tribunal (Objection!) with CREATE2 (salt 0), once. `creationCode` must be the committed one; the Tribunal reads its settings from this contract and Seasons finds it here."
          },
          "letterboxCodeHash()": {
            "notice": "keccak256 of the Letterbox's creation code (it takes no constructor arguments)."
          },
          "oracleAsset()": {
            "notice": "The Letterbox's settings, read by its constructor: the asset the oracle fee is paid in, and whether it mints that fee (Sepolia's open-mint test token; refused on chain id 1)."
          },
          "predict(bytes32)": {
            "notice": "The address `deployHook(salt, \u2026)` deploys to."
          },
          "predictLetterbox()": {
            "notice": "The address `deployLetterbox` deploys to."
          },
          "predictTribunal()": {
            "notice": "The address `deployTribunal` deploys to (zero when objections are off)."
          },
          "seed()": {
            "notice": "Opens trading: creates the pool (90-min launch window starts) and the first Cabal's era. The hook, the Letterbox and a committed Tribunal must exist (anyone may deploy each with the committed code), so no plea is ever recorded out of the Tribunal's reach (round 6)."
          },
          "tribunalCodeHash()": {
            "notice": "keccak256 of the Tribunal's creation code (no constructor arguments); zero means the launch has no objections."
          }
        },
        "version": 1
      }
    },
